        <p>GURSHON, 44, OLDHAM-STRT"tm 'AA NC LOOTER.</p>
        <p>ATE THE PROPERTY J MERCHANT. who was on! The goods are offered for sale consequence of death. Every art' rantee that no house in Manche house like it for four times tb remark that the carpets and floor cove's..., the rooms. I have arranged to F upply new ce.tpew linoleums. and whoever buys the lot will have perfect free- dom to select the same. The diuing room, drawing room. ' ant various bed rooms are furnished with goods of the best 'quality. All lask is for intending customers to inspect the lot, which 1 offer for £9B cash, warranted and delivered, or 5 ler cent extra on the deterred payment system.</p>
        <p>GERSHON'S UNIVERSAL FURNISHING- ARCADE. 44, Oldham-street, Manchester, next to the Adeiphi Bank.</p>
        <p>I ATE THE PHOPi?.RTY OF A CLERGYMAN.</p>
        <p>1-4 Such a nice smart Dining Room in Leather: Small chairs (padded back), couch, and tasy chairs to match, solid frames, spring stuffed. a dead bargain for £5 15s handsome side- board to match, with bevelled glass back, £4 18s. ; extending dining table, to match with extra leaf,3Bs.; large size carpet. bordered, and rug to match, 285.; overmantel. a perfect beauty, 305.; fender, dogs, and fire brasses, 136, the lot; or the entire dining-room lot as above for £l6 75., or five per L cent extra on the deferred payment system.</p>
        <p>GERSHON'S UNIVERSAL FURNISHING ARCA.DB, 44, Oldham-street, Manchester, next to the Adelphi Bank</p>
        <p>T ATE TUE PROPKRTY OF MRS. WOODWIN. ILJ A charming Suite,which I have re-covered in handsome saddle bags; the woodwork is second hand, covering new small chairs, easy chairs, and couch,all to match ; worth £l5; price now, £5 15s. Cabinet, Table, and Overmantel to match. makirg a charming lot for very little money, Add 5 per cent. if on the deferred payment system.</p>
        <p>GERSHON'S UNIVERSAL FURNISHING ARCADE, 44, Oldham-street, Manchester next to the Adelpht Bank.</p>
        <p>LATE THE PROPERTY OF A BANKRUPT SILY. MEKCIIANT. Without doubt the handsomest fittings for a dining-room ever seen. Money cannot buy better. \The small chairs are most hand,omely carved. '1 he lounge chairs and couch are all upholster din a real crocodile leather, everlasting wear. The handsome sideboard, overmantel. and large extending dining table are all in dark (neary black)Chimindale risaho- gany. I him informed they cost nearly £2OO ; can uoW be had for 68 guineas, I have also the drawing room, which is magnificent. and a number of bedroom suites. One suite is in real satinwooa. richly inlaid, and I know for a positive fact it cost two years since 250 guineas, and is now on offer for 85 guineas. Another massive suite in solid wal- nutwood cannot be described, it's quite equal to new, in fact, better, it cost £9s—the invoice is in my possession—can now , be had for 55 guineas, warranted and delivered.</p>
        <p>GERSHON'S UNIVERSAL FURNISHING ARCADE. 44, Oldhun-street, Manchest,r, next to the Adelphl Bank.</p>
        <p>LATE the PROPEiaY of an HOTEL PHIETOR. &amp; Number of Bedroom Suites. Each suite has a wardrobe with bevelled glass door, enclosed dressing-t-ble gites at- tached ; enclosed washstand, with marble slabdile back, and shaving mirror ; bedside cupboard, rail ad chirs. Ia the goods are Ash, Birch. Walnut. Mahogany, Cyprus, and other woods ; prices. 7,8, 10, 12. 15, and 18 guineas the suite. One Suite, with 61t. 6in. wardrobe and 4ft, toilets cost £4O. for Z 7 guineas, or 5 per cent. extra on the defense.' payment system.</p>
