        <p>JA NIESON'S RIDE.</p>
        <p>-- Authentic reco-da of this Distoriesl Event now reach fing!and, and the Crisis is virtually over. Peace and plenty agiin rule through the Golden Territory of the Iransvaal, and the act, of Dr. Jam*:son links this modern Hero inalienably to one of the Historic Incidents of the Century No Infringement of our neutrality Call be urged against Us in laying bare to the Liverpool publics sublet of stro:lg local interest and advantage. A rumour was current previously, but is only con- frtned with " Dr. Jim's" arrival, that his brave band of Volunteers had became possessed (prior to the Raid) of the redoubtable clothing manufacturtql especially for South Africa by Messrs. HENOONS- MIRO. &amp; RLLIS, UNIVERSITY HOUSE, Islington, Liverpool, and Digt, the Natural Wool Under- wear famous for sti2l climates, shipped to the South African Repuplic. as well as to the Char- tered Company's Territory, by Messrs. H BNOC HS- BURG &amp; ELLIS, was worn by the Doctor's heips -during tleir trying time. The Government Serge. (passing full test for shades, dyes, and strength) are kept in stock at University House. Messrs. RENOCIISBERG &amp; lIILIS are prepared to under- salie and execute ORDERS tor GENTLEMEN'S SUITS fs.r 50e., ,or YOUTHS' SUITS 355., and for BOYS' SUITS 25e., from the exact materials, of which they now hold a ~00d selection, as the contract tor the betel Government is in course of oompletion by this weal-known lirm. ---------</p>
