      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-03-14_WidnesExaminer_art0073" n="art0073">
        <head>MAKE LIFE ENJOYABLE.</head>
        <p>MAKE LIFE ENJOYABLE.</p>
        <p>Loss of health means loss of all which makes life en- joyable ; for, in addition to the bodily pain and suffering which it causer:, it entails a vast amount of mental pain and anx:ety, especially in the homes of the working classes. It brings in its train a host of discomforts which retard the recovery 9f the sufferer, and hinder, instead of assisting, Nature to perform her functions. When a working man suffers from any ailment which prevents his following his daily avocation, he is natur- ally filled with anxiety regarding the maintenanco of those depending on him for their daily sustenance. B 6 very love for his family retards and hinders his speedy recovery, and his spirits become depres: ed at the antici- pation of the gloomy prospects before them in the event of a long continuance of his illness*. It is well known that depression of spirits often proves a serious bar to a speedy recovery. These results arise in addition to the various incon- veniences and discomforts which the sufferer and his family experience as direct results of his illness, such as additional expenses for luxuries for the sick, with in- creased difficulty to obtain those luxuries, or even the necessities of life.</p>
        <p>Meat of hevarjous form eF w6ocu,e which trouble the labouring classes of the country, and which are often attributt4nle, more or less, to some unhealthly condition of their daily work, may be classed under a tew leading heads.</p>
        <p>To avoid th,s discotnforts arising from valions forms .of diseasetevery working man shGuld seek thn aid of</p>
        <p>WILY M EVA.N'S QUININE BITTERS.</p>
        <p>THE VEGETABLE TONIC,</p>
        <p>Which has gained a world-wide renown as the tno-t wonderful medicinal discovery of the age; and as un- failing remedy it is prescribed by many leading physi- cians in various ailments.</p>
        <p>For Bronchitis, Asthma, Coughs, and Colds. Shortnesa e Breath, Neuralgia, General Weakness, Low Spirits, Nervousnes3, Indigestion, Influenza.</p>
      </div>
