        <p>IVERPOOL WINTER ASSIZES, MARCH, 1898 The Commissions for holding these Assizes will be opened at Liverpool on Monday, the 9th March. The Court will sit on Tuesday. the 10th March, at 11 &amp;clock a.m. and on every other day during the Assizes at 10 o'clock ualess otherwise directed. Bail cases ail! be taken at these Assizes. The Prosecutors and Witnesses in the after-mentioned cases are required to be in attendance at the times specified in the following List, and not earlier, and on all subsequent days, at the sitting ot the Court ; and the trials are to pro- ceed in the order in which the cases are arranged in the List, unless the Court shall otherwise direct. viz. On TUESDAY. the 10th March, at 11 o'clock a.m. The Queen v. Thomas Williams, post-office case; Samuel Williams. criminal assault; John Turner, criminal assault ; John flenshaw. wounding; Arthur Thomson, criminal as- sault ; Neville Waghorn, forgery; Stephen Bailey, forgery John Quinlan. wounding; George Goulding. wounding; Wil- liam Cavanogh and others. robbery; William Miller and others, burglary; John Shea and another, robbery; James Bleasdale and another, burglary ;John McGuiness and others, robbery; Cornelius Mangan and another. wounding; Joseph Moder and another, robbery ; Roslna Emily Hunter, higamy; William Davies, worinding ; James Berry, robbery ; James Stewart, bigamy; Thomas Jennings, robbery ; William Thompson. burglary; Edward Connolly, burglary; James Greaves and another, Mint case; William Hyndman, wound- ing ; John Thomas Hamilton, criminal assault; Arthur Kay and another, robbery; Mary Ann Warburton and others, burglary ; Ernest Plumpton, criminal assault; Leslie Ken- nedy. burglary; John Sinclare. criminal assault; Richard McCauley, wounding; Michael King, robbery; John Marsh and another, neglecting children ; Robert Lyon, burglary; Michael White, wounding; William Shorroctx, false pretences; James Champerlorier, criminal assault; Alfred Radcliffe, wounding; John Doherty and another, burglary. On WEDN ESDAY. the 11th March, at 10 o'clock a.m. The Queen •. Thomas Rodwell, criminal assault; John Marrow, criminal assault ; Marcus Wienbact conspiring, Ac.; Abraham Kezler and another, conspiracy ; Robert Foster, manslaughter ; John McMahon, criminal assault ; George Leatherharrow and another. manslaughter, Ac ; Herbert Westworth, murder; Peter Hookey. manslaughter; John; Cavanagh. criminal assault ; Thomas Brady. criminal assault William nape, manslaughter ; William Bentham, periur• ; Wills harper, forgery • lda Mary Maloney Baxter, murder ; Patrick Kelly, criminal assault; Edward Magrath, forgery James Sloan, arson. And all other Cases. All Indictments settled by Counsel must be forwarded to me Engrossed and abstracted. The foregoing Regulations will be strictly enforced, and persons making default in the observance of them will be liable to have their costs disallowed. HEREF.RT STEPHEN, Clerk of Assize. Office of Clerk of Assize, Preston. 4th March, 1895. N.B.—lt is particularly requested that all Depositions, In- quisitions, and Recoguntaneas may be immediately forwarded to me at Preston.</p>
