        <p>WARRINGTON UNION. —Persons willing to CONTRACT for the supply of any of the undermentioned articles from Lady Day to Michaelmas to be delivered free of expense at the Warrington Union Workhouse, or at the Industrial Schools, Padgste, at such times and in such quantities as the Board of Guardians shall direct, are requested to send in TBNDERS,properly sealed,endorsed, and tree of expense, ad- dressed to the Clerk to the Guardians, between four o'clock p.m., on Tuesday, the 17th day of March inst. The following are the articles for which tenders are re- quired Groceries and Provisions Shoes, Clogs and Slippers Beef and Mutton Glazing Joints for Officers Brushes Flwir and Irish pin head Meal Coffins Loaves of Bresd Best, Oakum Rope for picking Beer and Porter Best Penmftenmavrr Stone Straw and Potatoes for breaking purposes Drapery. Ac Leather Cord aid Twill Wood for cutting into Fire- Coal Slack Bnd Gas Coke wood Earthenware Samples of any of the above may be seen on application to the Master of the Workhouse. The Coal and Slack supplied mutt beta the satisfaction of the House ant Schools Commit- tee, The Pit and quality of Coal must be named in the Ten- der. Forms Of tender and full particulars as to the probable quantities of each article required may be obtained at the Clerk's Office. Each tender must be made upon the prescribed form and roperly enclosed ant endorsed with the name of the artiele tendered for. Each article tenderel for must be of the size ma erial,and quAlity shown at the Workhouse or Schools. No Traders for other articles will be accepted. Bach cmtractor must be prepared (if required) to enter into security for the due'performance of his contract. The Guardians do not bind hemselves to accept the lowest or any tender. All contract _accounts will be paid quarterly.—BY order. JAMES CLOWES SUTTON. Clerk to the Guardians, Bewsey Chambers, Warrington, March sth, 1696.</p>
        <p>RUNCORN UNION.—CONTRACTS for PROVI- SIONS and SUPPLIES for the Half-year ending October 3rd, 1896. The GUARDIANS of the POOR of the RUNCORN UNION are desirorts of receiving TENDERS from parties willing to Contract for the supply of New Milk, Buttermilk, Fresh Butter and Fresh Eggs (for twelve months), Flour, Oatmeal, Groceries, Peas, Cheese, Salt Butter ; Cod Liver and Paraffin Oil •, Quinine ; good Beef to consist of vein pieces intact and list Ribs with Bone ; one Round weekly not to exceed 251bs. and 50Ibs. per week of the best Butcher's Meat for the Officers, and Sides of Mutton ; Bread ; Home-cured Bacon ; Potatoes ; Wheat Straw ; Drapery and Clothing ; Men's, Women's, Boys' and Girls' Shoes of various sizes, as per samples, to be seen at the Workhouse, Dutton, and Shoe Mending ; House Coal (Colliery to be named) ; good Deal Coffins, specifying size and including plate with name, age, and date of death.to be delivered in the Union when and where required ; Coke; Carting at per mile, Funerals at per Funeral. Parties tendering for the supply of the above-mentioned Goods, will be required to deliver the same at the Workhouse, free of cost to the Guardians, how And when required. Tenders to be accompanied with Samples (except Drapery Goods), as far as practicable. The Guardians do not bind themselves to accept the Lowest or any Tender. Persons desirous of Tendering must apply by letter to my office in Runcorn, for a printed Form of Tender (and none other can be entertained), where a Schedule of the various articles required and further particulars may be obtained. Sealed Tenders neidressed to the Guardians, to be for- warded to the Clerk's Office, Runcorn, on or before Monday, ttle 16th day of March, 1896, endorsed "Tender for" The Tenders will be opened and considered at a Meeting of the Guardians to be held in the Boardroom, Dutton, on the 17th day ot March. 1896, at 12-30 p.m. Parties whose Tenders are accepted must enter into a voitten Contract, and be prepared to enter into a Bond with two sureties, if required by the Guardians. By order of the Board. JOHN Asurox, Clerk to the Guardians. lt,incorn, 3rd March, 1896.</p>
