        <p>MARRIAGES. BRAMHALL—CLARE—February 29th. at the Parish Church. Warrington, by the Rev H It M Hutt, Edward Bramhall to Alice Clare. FAIRBROTHER—HARDING—FebrUary 29th, At the Parish Church Warrington, by the Rev /1 It M Hutt, James Fair- brother to Elizabeth Harding, DEATHS. FORSTER.—March 3, at Halton. Betty Forster, widow of the late Thomas Forster, seed 76 years. ROBE ATT.—February 27th, at Pierpoint-st., Warrington. Catherine Roberts, aged 31 years. HARDY.—February 28th, at Lloyd-st., Warrington. Ellen Hardy, aged 7 yea's. CoNnoY.—February 29th. at Upper Bank-st., Warrington' John Conroy, aged 56 years. Minnocx.—'narch Ist, at Marsh-at., Warrington, Annie Peacock Maddock, aged 37 years. WALL.—March 2nd, at Collins-st., Warrington, James Wall. aged 46 years. DENNErr.—March 4th, at Factory Yard, Warrington, Mari Dennett, aged 51 years. IN MEMORIAM. BULLOCK—In Memoriam of Sarah Lucy Bullock, who died March Bth, 1895. "Gone but not forgotten." IN MRMORIAM. In loving memory of JonN ERlNnonnix, who fell asleep oil March 13th, 1895. Gone but not forgotten. IN MEMORiAm. VERNON—In Loving Memory of Louisia Vernon, who (Rea March 6th, 1895. "Gone but not forgotton."</p>
